{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Who would have said to Abraham.</b> An expression of praise and importance — see, who He is and how great He is, who keeps His promise: the Holy One, blessed be He, promises and fulfills." "<b>Said.</b> Scripture changed and did not say דִּבֵּר — its gematria is 100, that is, at the end of a hundred years to Abraham." "<b>Sarah nursed children.</b> And what is בָּנִים in the plural? On the day of the feast, the noblewomen brought their children with them and she nursed them — for people were saying, Sarah did not give birth, rather she brought a foundling from the marketplace."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:59:41.798513576Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}